1337 Update Log
===============


v3.0.0.1 (Pre Release)

Builds on current systems: OpenSSL 3, Boost 1.66 to 1.92, GCC 13+, Clang/Xcode, Qt 5.15, miniupnpc 2.2.8+
Added - GitHub Actions builds for Linux, Windows and macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel)
Faster sync - 500 blocks per getblocks request (was 50)
Faster sync - sync peer is chosen and replaced when it stalls or disconnects (was the first peer to connect, forever)
Faster sync - stall watchdog asks again after 60s without a new block, switches peer after two stalls
Fix - sync paused after every batch past block 17280: peers pointed downloaders back at their last proof-of-work block (17280, the end of PoW) to continue, which got nothing new; now they point at their best block, and the wallet continues from its own tip when an older peer still names 17280 (local test: 185s -> 8s)
Faster sync - if the sync peer goes quiet for 5s after a batch, the wallet asks for the next batch itself instead of waiting for a new network block
Faster sync - blocks offered by the sync peer are requested immediately (no 2 minute retry delay)
Faster sync - larger database cache by default (-dbcache=100)
Faster sync - sync peer is picked from the tallest peers (newer wallets first among them), not a peer that is itself still syncing
Faster sync - moves on right away when the sync peer has no more blocks and another peer is ahead (it used to wait forever)
Faster sync - no more walking back to the sync-checkpoint for every new block
Faster sync - each block's X11 hash is computed once instead of every time it is needed
Faster sync - blocks aren't announced to other peers while still catching up
Added - debug.log line every 1000 blocks while syncing: blocks per second and time spent checking blocks
Added - getpeerinfo: knownheight (highest block the peer is known to have)
Wallet look - sync bar shows the time left (e.g. "about 2 h 10 min left"); tooltip has blocks per second and blocks to go
Memory - orphan blocks capped (-maxorphanblocksmib, default 40)
Memory - getdata requests answered as the send buffer drains instead of all at once
Memory - old block/transaction requests are forgotten; per-peer request queue capped
Memory - orphan transaction pool limited to 1000
Fix - key copies kept the wrong compressed flag; bad keys leaked memory
Fix - MultiSend tried to send a transaction that failed to be created
Fix - MultiSend: a disabled address no longer stops MultiSend for every other stake; a split stake no longer ends the loop early; your split-stake setting is no longer switched off for good
Fix - change could go to a random address on some send paths (a coin control setting was never set)
Changed - change goes back to the address it came from, so a wallet backup always holds the change (-returnchange=0 for a new address each time); key pool is 1000 keys (was 100)
Fix - -testnet failed at startup (genesis block)
Added - -blockbatchsize option
Added - RPC: getblockchaininfo, getblockheader, gettxout, gettxoutsetinfo, getmempoolinfo, getnetworkhashps, getsupply, getmaxmoney
Added - RPC: getnetworkinfo, getnettotals, ping, addnode, getaddednodeinfo, disconnectnode, setban, listbanned, clearbanned, uptime
Added - RPC: getwalletinfo, getdescriptorinfo, deriveaddresses
Fix - addnode: works without -addnode at startup, re-resolves names, doesn't wait for an outbound slot
Fix - getinfo includes moneysupply (block explorers read it)
Fix - duplicate keys in transaction and block JSON
Changed - RPC accepts true/false or 1/0 for verbose options, and numbers given as strings
Changed - getpeerinfo: id, ping time, bytes sent/received, addnode, syncnode
Wallet look - overview page rebuilt to the Elite design; it fits any window size instead of one fixed picture
Wallet look - the window can be resized (was fixed at 960x710) and remembers its size; sharp on high-DPI screens
Wallet look - fonts come with the wallet (Oswald, Pinyon Script), so it looks the same on every computer
Wallet look - page links across the top with the menus under them; MultiSend added to the links
Wallet look - gold sync progress bar across the bottom of the window
Wallet look - lock button on the overview: shows locked/unlocked/not encrypted, click to unlock, lock or encrypt
Wallet look - the recent transactions list shows as many as fit; Discord and X links on the overview
Wallet look - new theme file 1337-4.qss (an old 1337-3.qss in the data directory is no longer used)
Removed - unused images and icons
Fix - the wallet crashed on its first start (the wallet file name was empty in the settings migration)
Faster sync - blocks are processed as soon as they arrive (the message thread no longer sleeps 100 ms between batches)
Faster sync - the sync peer target is a height at least two peers agree on, so one peer claiming a fake height can't pull the wallet off course
Changed - 3.0 or newer wallets are always picked to download the block chain from, and replace an older sync peer as soon as one connects; older wallets are used only when no 3.0+ wallet is connected (temporary, until most users run 3.0+)
Changed - debug.log shows each peer's wallet version when it connects
Changed - block files are 25 MiB each in a "chain" folder (as on FlapX); existing blk*.dat files are moved there on first start, no resync needed
Fix - no staking and no stake weight calculation while the wallet is still downloading the chain (before, a pause of 10 seconds between blocks, or getting past the last checkpoint, could make it start staking on an old block)
Fix - the window never waits on the core for the balance or staking icon, and checks the balance every 10 seconds while syncing instead of on every block
Changed - the block number in the wallet updates 10 times a second while syncing (was twice a second)
Fix - addresses that keep failing are retried less and less often (1, 2, 4 ... minutes, at most an hour apart) instead of every few seconds, so a wallet that knows only a few dead addresses stops hammering them
Faster sync - while far behind, the wallet stops serving blocks to others so it can catch up first
Fix - forks below the last checkpoint are rejected straight away
Changed - public IP is learned from what peers report (two peers in different networks must agree) instead of an old web lookup at a fixed address
Changed - UPnP looks a little further for the router
Fix - leftover peers.dat.XXXX temp files are cleaned up at startup and after a failed save
Added - Debug window: Peers tab (address, direction, version, height, ping, traffic; click a peer for details)
Added - Debug window: Network Traffic tab with a 10 minute graph and totals
Fix - a peer claiming a made-up block height could make a synced wallet stop handing out blocks to others; claimed heights are now capped at what's plausible, each network counts once, and a wallet whose newest block is under an hour old always serves
Added - sync bar tooltip shows blocks per second (right now and averaged over the last few minutes), from the start of the sync
Added - sync bar shows the download speed in blocks a minute next to the time left
Added - Elite Status on the overview changes with how much the wallet holds: Noob, Entrepreneur (500K), Millionaire (1M), Investor (10M), Magnate (100M), Mogul (250M), Tycoon (500M), Billionaire (1B), Elite (3B); hover it to see the next level
Changed - checkpoints and stake modifier checkpoints every 25,000 blocks up to 5,725,000 (230 of each), replacing the old irregular lists; read from a fully synced node, and every old checkpoint at the same height matched
Faster startup - "Loading block index" is quicker: the block index is a hash table instead of a sorted map (at full chain size, looking blocks up took about 8 seconds instead of 39 in a test), and each block's chain trust is worked out on every CPU core
Changed - window title shows Pre Release and the nightly date (11-18-2026 Nightly)
Changed - Overview: "Recent Transactions" sits above its box, so the box fits more transactions; dates, labels and amounts are in the balance's gold
Changed - Overview: the lock button turns gold (outline and text) while the wallet is unlocked
Fix - MultiSend: buttons are wide enough for their labels ("View MultiSend" and "Deactivate" were cut off)
Fix - menus: icons no longer touch the menu's left edge
Added - on first start the wallet writes 1337.conf with a random RPC user name and password, the RPC port and RPC limited to this computer; RPC stays off until you remove the # from server=1 (an existing 1337.conf is never changed)
Removed - old NovaCoin/Bitcoin packaging and art (Debian, Gitian, NSIS installer, bitmaps, Doxygen logo); Windows icon renamed elite.ico


